<title>UK: Export Finance sets 14 bln yen three-year bond.</title>
<headline>Export Finance sets 14 bln yen three-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers LTCB International Ltd and SBC Warburg.</p>
<p> BORROWER   EXPORT FINANCE AND INSURANCE CORP</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  AUSTRALIA</p>
<p> AMT   *14 BLN YEN    COUPON     5.42	MATURITY   *24.FEB.00</p>
<p> TYPE   DUAL-CURRENCY ISS PRICE  98.50     PAY DATE    24.FEB.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  20 BP     REOFFER    98.50     SPREAD	 =</p>
<p> NOTES     *REDEMPTION IN AUSTRLIAN DOLLARS.</p>
<p> MOODY    **AA2	 LISTING    NONE	PAY FREQ    SEMI-ANN</p>
<p> S&amp;P	**AA	  SALE LIMITS US/UK/JP/DE/AU</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> NOTES     **PROGRAMME AND BOND RATING BY S&amp;P BUT PROGRAMME</p>
<p>		 RATING ONLY BY MOODY'S .</p>
<p>		 ISSUED FROM A $1.5 BILLION EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
